As shown in Listing 2-9, there are lower-level reader functions called
from blo_read_file_internal(). Let us discuss two of them, read_
global() and read_libblock(), both static and defined in readfile.c.
At this level, the static functions no longer have the module prefix (here,
the lowercase blo_*). We have seen this already with the function read_
file_dna().
read_global() is used to gather version information from the blend
